NAME
    dump - display memory as hex

SYNOPSIS
    dump addr

DESCRIPTION
    Displays 256 bytes of memory starting at the hexadecimal address
    addr, as 16 rows of "AAAA: bb bb ... cccc" (hex bytes then their
    ASCII, non-printable shown as "."). After each block it waits for a
    console key: "." returns to the shell, any other key shows the next
    block. dump is a /bin program (formerly an OS built-in).

NOTES
    dump loads into the TPA at $7A00, so dumping that region shows dump's
    own bytes. It reads memory only -- see dep to change it.

EXAMPLES
    dump 7A00
    dump 4000        peek at the resident OS

SEE ALSO
    dep, load, save
